      "label": "text",
      "prov": [],
      "orig": "The C footprint for milk produced in the system was calculated using a biophysical allocation approach, as recommended by the International Dairy Federation [49], and described by Thoma et al. [48]. Briefly, ARmilk = 1–6.04 × BMR, where: ARmilk is the allocation ratio for milk and BMR is cow BW at the time of slaughter (kg) + calf BW sold (kg) divided by the total ECM produced during cow`s entire life (kg). The ARmilk were 0.854 and 0.849 for TMR and TMR with both pasture scenarios, respectively. The ARmilk was applied to the whole emissions, except for the electricity consumed for milking (milking parlor) and refrigerant loss, which was directly assigned to milk production.",
      "text": "The C footprint for milk produced in the system was calculated using a biophysical allocation approach, as recommended by the International Dairy Federation [49], and described by Thoma et al. [48]. Briefly, ARmilk = 1–6.04 × BMR, where: ARmilk is the allocation ratio for milk and BMR is cow BW at the time of slaughter (kg) + calf BW sold (kg) divided by the total ECM produced during cow`s entire life (kg). The ARmilk were 0.854 and 0.849 for TMR and TMR with both pasture scenarios, respectively. The ARmilk was applied to the whole emissions, except for the electricity consumed for milking (milking parlor) and refrigerant loss, which was directly assigned to milk production."
